%erg 0.1
Title: Add a gofmt + go vet adherence ratchet to the test suite
Created: 2026-06-03
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-06-03T03:35Z claude created
2026-06-03T05:10Z claude note corrected the root-cause framing. The version.go "drift" is NOT a corrupt/broken/padme-local gofmt (an earlier note wrongly said so). It is STOCK gofmt doc-comment smart-quoting: '' -> U+201D, two backticks -> U+201C (proposal #51082, Go 1.19+, in go/printer). A REAL gofmt on ANY machine, CI included, wants to rewrite version.go's `'\''` comment, which collides with the ASCII-only src/go guard. So `gofmt -l src/go/` is NOT clean anywhere today -- the rewording below is the prerequisite that makes the ratchet possible, not optional cleanup. Refs golang/go#61365, #76975.

--- body ---
## Context

git-erg has no mechanical Go-formatting/vet gate -- the analog of the Python
ruff adherence check the harness rules mandate. `make check` runs the suite +
corpus validation but never `gofmt -l` or `go vet`, so formatting drift only
gets caught by a human reviewer or /verify's ad-hoc pass. The /verify on PR
#242 (ticket 0207) flagged this gap directly.

Blocker for the ratchet (stock gofmt vs ASCII-only): gofmt's doc-comment
formatter applies Markdown-style smart quotes -- `''` becomes U+201D (a curly
right double quote) and two backticks become U+201C -- everywhere, in every
Go >= 1.19 (proposal #51082; complained about in golang/go#61365 and the
Dec-2025 #76975). `src/go/version.go`'s shellSingleQuote comment contains
`'\''` (ends in `''`), so ANY real gofmt -- CI's included, not just this
machine's -- wants to rewrite it to a non-ASCII `'\` + U+201D, which violates
the ASCII-only src/go guard (test_encoding, ticket 0167). So `gofmt -l
src/go/` is NOT clean today on any machine, and a naive `gofmt -w` would inject
non-ASCII. This is stock behaviour, NOT a corrupt or broken toolchain.

## Actions

1. Reword the smart-quote triggers out of Go comments FIRST: rewrite
   `src/go/version.go`'s shellSingleQuote comment (and grep for any other Go
   comment with the pair: `grep -RnP "''" src/go; grep -RnF '` + "``" + `' src/go`)
   so it conveys the same meaning without the literal `''` / two-backtick pair.
   Then gofmt's smart-quoting is a no-op and the comment stays ASCII.
2. Fix any genuine formatting drift gofmt surfaces (ref_test.go, refs_test.go,
   ...) with a real gofmt or by hand. NOTE: padme's gofmt is fine -- it is just
   stock smart-quoting; once step 1 removes the `''`, `gofmt -w` is safe here
   too. Re-check `grep -RP '[^\x00-\x7F]' src/go` after.
3. Add `tests/test_gofmt.sh`: assert `gofmt -l src/go/` prints nothing and
   `cd src/go && go vet ./...` exits 0. Register the suite in TEST_SUITES.

## Test

`tests/test_gofmt.sh` with a negative control (a deliberately mis-indented
temp .go file is reported by `gofmt -l`), so the ratchet is non-vacuous.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] No Go comment in src/go contains `''` or a two-backtick pair that gofmt
      would smart-quote (version.go reworded; grep clean).
- [ ] `gofmt -l src/go/` is clean on a real gofmt (so the gate passes in CI).
- [ ] `go vet ./...` clean.
- [ ] `tests/test_gofmt.sh` exists, registered in TEST_SUITES, with a passing
      negative control.
- [ ] `make check` passes; `grep -RP '[^\x00-\x7F]' src/go` stays empty.
